DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ppoossiixx__ssppaawwnnaattttrr__ggeettffllaaggss() function obtains the value of the spawn-
     flags attribute from the attributes object referenced by _a_t_t_r.

     The ppoossiixx__ssppaawwnnaattttrr__sseettffllaaggss() function sets the spawn-flags attribute in
     an initialized attributes object referenced by _a_t_t_r.

     The spawn-flags attribute is used to indicate which process attributes
     are to be changed in the new process image when invoking ppoossiixx__ssppaawwnn() or
     ppoossiixx__ssppaawwnnpp().  It is the bitwise-inclusive OR of zero or more of the
     following flags (see ppoossiixx__ssppaawwnn()):

           POSIX_SPAWN_RESETIDS

           POSIX_SPAWN_SETPGROUP

           POSIX_SPAWN_SETSIGDEF

           POSIX_SPAWN_SETSIGMASK

           POSIX_SPAWN_SETSCHEDPARAM

           POSIX_SPAWN_SETSCHEDULER

           POSIX_SPAWN_DISABLE_ASLR_NP

     These flags are defined in <_s_p_a_w_n_._h>.  The default value of this attri‐
     bute is as if no flags were set.

